https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2719478973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iF_S9","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T01:03:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T01:03:15Z","body":"I'll create a mrp from your instructions.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719478973/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719484656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2719484656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2719484656,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iGArw","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T01:08:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T01:13:10Z","body":"![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/af797ddc-aa9d-494d-af3a-624010bfff1a)\n\n[new-game-project-csg.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19219827/new-game-project-csg.zip)\n\nAs far as I can tell the CSG mesh is physically a rectangular prism and it shows. It's working in the sense that it's not empty. However it's also not working showing the subdivision.\n\nI think we should note in documentation the CSG keeps the shape but optimizes the shape. We discussed this in an earlier comment. ~~I'll try to find it.~~\n\nEdited:\n\nI can't find the comment about asking @elalish about how to disable optimizations.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719484656/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719947971","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2719947971","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2719947971,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iHxzD","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T04:55:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T05:11:11Z","body":"Personally, when interacting with CSG, I would expect that sometimes it will get rid of subdivisions and sometimes it will preserve them (or *appear* to preserve them) depending on how floating point inaccuracy affects that specific mesh.\n\nAs a shot in the dark: 1/128 is a perfectly representable number because 128 is a power of two, vs. 1/120 which produces an infinitely repeating pattern that must be truncated to fit in our floating point representation. The truncation gets rid of some accuracy, and the CSG system might see a \"bumpy\" surface.\n\nIn general, I expect a CSG system to \"optimize\" the mesh when the numbers are accurate (representable). I don't really see it as optimization: CSG systems seem to me to work at a higher level than meshes, on \"solid geometry\", where subdivisions aren't important. I don't expect the subdivisions to necessarily even show up in the internal representation used by the CSG system, and depending on how it's implemented, it might be a lot of work to keep them around.\n\nBut: these are only my opinions on how I've come to expect a CSG system to operate in general. Everyone uses CSG for different reasons and has different expectations.\n\n---\n\nI'm curious what the use case is. What do the subdivisions help with in the world of CSG? (Or do they come into play post-CSG?)\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719947971/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720021806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2720021806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2720021806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iID0u","user":{"login":"aristides86","id":18696109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Njk2MTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18696109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86","html_url":"https://github.com/aristides86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T05:23:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T05:30:04Z","body":"My use case is to create a water surface and another csg to cut a hole for the boat. Then I'm using water shader to move the vertices around without water clipping through the bottom of athe boat, so I do need vertices for that.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/053f8eab-e383-49c9-90c8-75626939f89e)\n\nThis is a screenshot from 4.3's csg system.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62939120-725d-44b2-9cb3-acb0f63957ad)\n\nAs I mentioned, the size 128 just disappears and I get the empty shape warning. If this is supposed behavior, then it is unclear what is expected from user.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720021806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720046259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2720046259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2720046259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iIJyz","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T05:42:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T05:44:43Z","body":"Thanks! I hadn't considered wanting to keep them around for a vertex shader.\n\n> [Node configuration warning screenshot]\n> \n> As I mentioned, the size 128 just disappears and I get the empty shape warning. If this is supposed behavior, then it is unclear what is expected from user.\n\nCan you share that scene as the MRP? It seems quite different from the original issue, which was only an issue with the mesh (it existing but leaving out the subdivisions), but maybe I'm not understanding something.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720046259/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720053468","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2720053468","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2720053468,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iILjc","user":{"login":"aristides86","id":18696109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Njk2MTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18696109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86","html_url":"https://github.com/aristides86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T05:48:14Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T05:48:14Z","body":"[csg_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19223100/csg_test.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720053468/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720096658","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2720096658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2720096658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iIWGS","user":{"login":"elalish","id":1649964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDk5NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1649964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish","html_url":"https://github.com/elalish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elalish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T06:18:08Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T06:18:08Z","body":"Yes, we've had enough people asking for this (not automatically collapsing coplanar geometry) that we're changing how Manifold operates in this arena. Part of it is already done and I'm in the middle o