github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885169917","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2885169917","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2885169917,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r-DL9","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-15T22:15:37Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T00:52:50Z","body":"@aristides86 \n\nAn infinitely flat plane (quad) doesn't have a volume so it doesn't fit the definition of https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/3d/csg_tools.html#custom-meshes\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885169917/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885210923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2885210923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2885210923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r-NMr","user":{"login":"aristides86","id":18696109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Njk2MTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18696109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86","html_url":"https://github.com/aristides86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aristides86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-15T22:43:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-15T22:43:52Z","body":"@fire thank you, that looks great \n\nAbout the plane - I get it, it doesn't have a volume, but still I don't see why it is not possible to make a plane CSG. What I mean is, a plane is just the top part of a cube. So, to make plane an CSG geometry, all we need is to take a cube, do all the boolean business with it and then remove everything below the top plane. As a result we get a flat plane with a boolean operation on it.\n\nWhatever the case is, using a cube instead of a plane, lets say for a terrain, is just not optimal because it doubles the amount of polygons used for that terrain. But I'm sure this tool is not really supposed to be used like that, it's mostly for grey boxing to be later replaced by optimal meshes. Users can always just import a MeshInstance. For me, it just would be nice to have realtime holes in water plane during gameplay so that boats don't look like they're sinking ,and this tool was the only solution for that.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885210923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885687623","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2885687623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2885687623,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sABlH","user":{"login":"cloudofoz","id":120678869,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzFp1Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120678869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz","html_url":"https://github.com/cloudofoz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T05:38:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T05:38:40Z","body":"Hi, I'm the author of the [smash-the-mesh](https://github.com/cloudofoz/godot-smashthemesh) addon, which uses CSG. I've tested it with Godot 4.4+ and everything works great, so thanks to everyone working on the CSG system!\n\nThe only limitation I've run into is that some meshes, like Blender’s Suzanne or the Godot plush mesh, no longer seem to be supported. I believe this is due to them not being fully manifold.\n\nIt might be helpful to expose a GDScript method to check if a mesh is manifold, so developers can catch and warn about these issues programmatically. That way, we can provide clearer feedback to users when something breaks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885687623/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885736049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2885736049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2885736049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sANZx","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T06:11:05Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T06:11:27Z","body":"I agree, the problem I had was the scene tree warnings would spam so I only made a notice when there was an empty mesh. Feel free to amend ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885736049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885885482","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104048#issuecomment-2885885482","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104048","id":2885885482,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sAx4q","user":{"login":"cloudofoz","id":120678869,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzFp1Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120678869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz","html_url":"https://github.com/cloudofoz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cloudofoz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T07:28:14Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T07:28:14Z","body":"You suggested a good workaround without needing any engine changes, thanks!\n\nCalling `get_meshes()` programmatically and checking if it returns null could be a simple way to detect unsupported (i.e. non-manifold) meshes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885885482/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]